{"comment_text": {"ja66:0.1": "", "ja66:0.2": "", "ja66:0.3": "", "ja66:0.4": "", "ja66:1.1": "An ascetic desires the queen, but when he gains her he finds that his list of desires does not shrink but grows. ", "ja66:1.2": "", "ja66:1.3": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Aḷārakkhī</i> is unique. More commonly we find <i lang='pi' translate='no'>aḷārapamha</i>, where, as here <i lang='pi' translate='no'>aḷāra</i> is glossed as <i lang='pi' translate='no'>visāla</i>, “wide”. Compare Sanskrit <i lang='pi' translate='no'>arāḍa</i>, glossed with <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ucchritaśṛṅga</i>, “high-horned”. I think it describes wide-open, expressive eyes (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>akkhī</i>) with eyebrows (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>pamha</i>) that are high and curved like horns. ", "ja66:1.4": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Vijāyatha</i> is reflexive third singular aorist, glossed with <i lang='pi' translate='no'>janesi</i>. ", "ja66:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja66:0.1": "<article id='ja66'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja66:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja66:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja66:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja66:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja66:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja66:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja66:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja66:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja66:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja66:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja66:0.3": "Itthivagga ", "ja66:0.4": "6. Mudulakkhaṇajātaka ", "ja66:1.1": "“Ekā icchā pure āsi, ", "ja66:1.2": "aladdhā mudulakkhaṇaṁ; ", "ja66:1.3": "Yato laddhā aḷārakkhī, ", "ja66:1.4": "icchā icchaṁ vijāyathā”ti. ", "ja66:2.1": "Mudulakkhaṇajātakaṁ chaṭṭhaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja66:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 66 ", "ja66:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja66:0.3": "Women ", "ja66:0.4": "Queen Sweetheart: a past life story ", "ja66:1.1": "One wish I had in the past, ", "ja66:1.2": "before I won Queen Sweetheart. ", "ja66:1.3": "But when I won the moon-eyed lady, ", "ja66:1.4": "wish upon wish was born. ", "ja66:2.1": ""}, "reference_text": {"ja66:0.1": "", "ja66:0.2": "", "ja66:0.3": "", "ja66:0.4": "", "ja66:1.1": "bj30.28, ms22J_145, msdiv66, pts-vp-pli1.306", "ja66:1.2": "", "ja66:1.3": "", "ja66:1.4": "", "ja66:2.1": "ms22J_146"}, "keys_order": ["ja66:0.1", "ja66:0.2", "ja66:0.3", "ja66:0.4", "ja66:1.1", "ja66:1.2", "ja66:1.3", "ja66:1.4", "ja66:2.1"]}